pref-intro-general-title = Connection and use
pref-intro-general-description = Install and sign in to your provider, then choose it here. Program paths, the workspace, and service ports are handled automatically.
pref-intro-claude-title = Claude Code
pref-intro-claude-description = Finds the local Claude Code installation and reuses its CLI login. Custom API and connection options are in Advanced settings.
pref-intro-codex-title = Codex
pref-intro-codex-description = Finds the local Codex installation and reuses its CLI login. Custom API and connection options are in Advanced settings.
pref-intro-deepseek-title = DeepSeek Harness
pref-intro-deepseek-description = Finds DeepSeek Harness and inherits existing environment variables. If no key is configured, enter DEEPSEEK_API_KEY in Advanced settings. The official service does not need a custom API URL.
pref-intro-mcp-title = Connect research tools
pref-intro-mcp-description = Library tools are built in. Add and test other services here when you need them.
pref-intro-skills-title = Research workflows
pref-intro-skills-description = Enable built-in workflows or import your own instructions. Review imported skills before enabling them; use the match test to check when they activate.
pref-intro-diagnostics-title = Connection diagnostics
pref-intro-diagnostics-description = Refresh service status, restart runtimes, or export logs to investigate connection problems.
pref-mcp-add-sse = Add SSE
pref-advanced = Advanced settings
pref-advanced-description = These are optional overrides. By default, the workspace is under your Zotero profile, Node.js is detected automatically, and proxy settings are inherited from the process environment. Service ports are managed automatically.
pref-provider-advanced-description = Only needed for a custom installation or connection. Clear the path to detect it again. These environment variables override the general settings.
